    <section class="msc-learn-key-terms" aria-labelledby="MscGuide031Terms"><h2 id="MscGuide031Terms">Key Terms</h2><dl><div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Soft fork</dt><dd>A consensus change that makes previously valid behavior invalid under new rules.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Consensus</dt><dd>The shared validation rules independently enforced by Bitcoin nodes.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>BIP</dt><dd>A Bitcoin Improvement Proposal that documents a proposed standard, process, or protocol change.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Validation</dt><dd>The process of checking transactions and blocks against applicable rules.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Protocol</dt><dd>A defined set of rules and message formats that allows independent participants or software systems to interact consistently.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Node</dt><dd>Bitcoin software that communicates with peers and may validate, relay, store, or serve network data.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Proof of work</dt><dd>The computational process miners use to produce block hashes below the network target.</dd></div></dl></section>
